  "problem": "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=2z,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4pz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis and $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
